# Secrets for local development. Copy to `.env`, which is gitignored.
# Full instructions, including how to create each of these: see setup.md
#
# ── Nuxt Studio, the content editor at /_studio ────────────────────────────
# Two ways in — pick one, not both.
#
# A) A fine-grained personal access token. Simplest for one person editing
#    their own repo. Needs only Contents: read and write on this repository.
#    github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens
STUDIO_GITHUB_TOKEN=

# B) A GitHub OAuth app. Use this if more than one person will edit, so each
#    signs in as themselves. github.com/settings/developers
#    Callback URL must be exactly:
#      http://localhost:4321/__nuxt_studio/auth/github
#
#    Note the names. Some docs pages say NUXT_STUDIO_AUTH_GITHUB_*, which the
#    module does not read. These are the ones it looks for.
STUDIO_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
STUDIO_GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
